<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu'l-Aswar Shavur I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1049–1067</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu'l-Aswar Shavur I was the Shaddadid emir of Ganja in the south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> from 1049 to 1067, having earlier ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a>. A forceful soldier and patron, he fought and allied in turn with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, and accepted Seljuk overlordship. Ganja prospered under him as a market city on the routes linking the Caspian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p></div>
